@page "/icon-catalogue"

<PageTitle>Font Awesome Blazor Icon Catalogue</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid mt-3 mb-4">
    <h1>Icon catalogue</h1>

    <p>
        Every icon is addressed with a CSS class such as <code>fa-house</code>. On top of that raw form
        the library gives you two compile-time checked shortcuts, so a renamed icon becomes a build
        error instead of a silently blank glyph:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Typed constants</strong> from <code>Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor</code> — grouped as
            <code>IconNames.Solid</code>, <code>IconNames.Regular</code>, and
            <code>IconNames.Brands</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Preset components</strong> from the optional
            <code>Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor.Icons</code> package — one component per icon
            (<code>HouseIcon</code>, <code>GithubIcon</code>, &hellip;) that bakes in the icon name and its
            primary Free style while leaving every style, size, transform, animation, and accessibility
            parameter overridable.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>Install the optional preset package:</p>

    <CodeSnippet Language="none">
        <Snippet>
            dotnet add package Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor.Icons
        </Snippet>
    </CodeSnippet>

    <p>
        Looking for an icon you only half remember? Use the <a class="link-primary" href="icon-browser">icon browser</a> to
        search by name, alias, or keyword.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="icon-catalogue-page sample-page">
    <SampleTabs>
        <Tabs>
            <SampleTab Text="Blazor">
                <Samples>
                    <Sample CssClass="mb-5" SnippetComponent=typeof(IconNamesSnippet) Heading="Typed constants" />
                    <Sample CssClass="mb-5" SnippetComponent=typeof(PresetComponentsSnippet) Heading="Preset components" />
                </Samples>
            </SampleTab>
        </Tabs>
    </SampleTabs>
</div>

<div class="container-fluid mt-4 mb-5">
    <h2>Which one should I use?</h2>

    <table class="table table-striped align-middle">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Approach</th>
                <th>Package</th>
                <th>Typical use</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>IconName="fa-house"</code></td>
                <td><code>Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor</code></td>
                <td>Dynamic names, data-driven markup, no extra dependency.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>IconName="@@IconNames.Solid.House"</code></td>
                <td><code>Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor</code></td>
                <td>Compile-time checked name, autocomplete and rename refactoring.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>&lt;HouseIcon /&gt;</code></td>
                <td><code>Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor.Icons</code></td>
                <td>Shortest markup, correct default style baked in.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
